# SHA-256 of every upstream byte this package compiles, installs, reads as
# an oracle, or publishes terms for, from PCRE2 10.49 (tag pcre2-10.49, commit
# 6f9d7c1373262c541324a16a358785b33ef116cf, https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2.git),
# plus this fork's own fixture module.
#
# 59 records, in this exact path set:
#
#   30  src/*.c        the explicit core_sources list in build.zig:90-121
#    1  src/pcre2_chartables.c.dist
#                      the generated character tables; upstream ships them under a
#                      .dist name and build.zig:486-494 copies it to
#                      pcre2_chartables.c and compiles that
#    2  src/pcre2posix.c, src/pcre2test.c
#                      the two further artifacts this graph builds
#    2  src/pcre2.h.generic, src/config-cmake.h.in
#                      the public header copied to pcre2.h and installed, and the
#                      config.h template
#   12  the internal headers the core includes: pcre2_internal.h, pcre2_compile.h,
#       pcre2_intmodedep.h, pcre2_ucp.h, pcre2_util.h, pcre2_jit_char_inc.h,
#       pcre2_jit_match_inc.h, pcre2_jit_misc_inc.h, pcre2_jit_simd_inc.h,
#       pcre2_printint_inc.h, pcre2_ucptables_inc.h, pcre2posix.h
#    3  LICENCE.md, COPYING, AUTHORS.md
#    8  testdata/testinput2, testoutput2, testinput5, testoutput5, testinput6,
#       testoutput6, testinput15, testoutput15
#                      the upstream pcre2test input and expected-output pairs that
#                      testdata/foundation-fixtures.zig cites by file and line
#    1  testdata/foundation-fixtures.zig
#                      NOT upstream's: this fork's own fixture module. It holds
#                      every expected answer the tests compare against, so a
#                      silent edit to it would move the oracle rather than break a
#                      build, and hashing it makes such an edit fail loudly.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   .gitignore        upstream's list is kept verbatim and this fork appends to it
#                     (.gitignore:130-157), so the file is not byte-identical to
#                     upstream's. The append is recorded in NOTICE.md.
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, translate.h, zig/, tests.zig, smoke.zig, consumer/,
#   cross-test.profile.sh, .github/workflows/verify.yml, UPSTREAM.md, NOTICE.md, CHANGELOG.md,
#   FORK-NOTES.md, README.zig.md
#                     this fork's own files, listed in NOTICE.md.
#   UPSTREAM.sha256    a record cannot contain its own digest.
#   the rest of testdata/
#                     upstream ships it whole and .paths ships it whole, but only
#                     the eight files above are cited line by line by the fixture
#                     module. The rest travel for provenance and for upstream's
#                     own RunTest; nothing in this package reads them.
#   the rest of src/   config.h.generic, config.h.in, pcre2.h.in, libpcre2-*.sym.in,
#                     the two EBCDIC character-table variants, pcre2demo.c,
#                     pcre2grep.c, pcre2posix_test.c, pcre2test_inc.h,
#                     pcre2_fuzzsupport.c, pcre2_jit_test.c -- none is compiled by
#                     this graph, read by the facade, or used as a test oracle.
#
# Method: each file was read as a raw byte read (Bun file.arrayBuffer) and hashed
# with SHA-256 from node:crypto, in an eval cell, on 2026-10-01. No shell hashing
# command and no git command was used. No receipt in this package's set reports
# the hashing tool's version, so this states the method and claims no version of
# it. Every one of the 59 records was then re-derived from the written file with
# the same method and compared against it.
#
# What this record establishes: if it validates, the bytes a build compiles, the
# header it translates, the licence a redistributor must reproduce and the oracle
# bytes the tests compare against are the bytes pinned here, and any later edit to
# one of them fails the check loudly.
#
# What it does not establish: it is not a signature, not a Git object id, and not
# a re-derivation from commit 6f9d7c1373262c541324a16a358785b33ef116cf. It is a
# hash of this working tree. That the tree equals that commit rests on the import
# and on the `git archive` digest in UPSTREAM.md, both recorded by the driver.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
# Current source/fetched replay status is driver-owned, outside these package bytes:
# FORKS.json.cross_test_wave.materialized_packages.pcre2 and
# local://foundation-cross-test-package-regression.json.
